                <pb facs="0621" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-05T12:00:00+08:00">March 5,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 5—2:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>306. Following from American Consul General, Mukden: <pb facs="0622" n="518"
                        xml:id="pg518"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 4, 5 p.m. Chao, Mayor of Mukden, in a press interview today,
                            stated that Chang Ching-hui would go to Tangkangtze, 60 miles south of
                            Mukden on the 7th where he will meet ex-Emperor Hsuan-tung who is to be
                            brought for this purpose from Port Arthur, and make the third request
                            that he ‘resume the post’. Chao stated that it is expected he must
                            accept the proposal and that he will proceed to Changchun where the
                            installation ceremony will take place on the 9th. The 10th, 11th, 12th
                            will be declared holidays throughout the provinces.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
